Given an array of n integers and a positive integer k, determine the number of (i,j) pairs where i<j  and a[i]+a[j]  is divisible by k.
input
6 3             n = 6, k = 3
1 3 2 6 1 2 
output
5
explanation
(0,2) --> a[0]+a[2]=1+2=3
(0,5) --> a[0]+a[5]=1+2=3
(1,3) --> a[1]+a[3]=3+6=3
(2,4) --> a[2]+a[4]=2+1=3
(4,5) --> a[4]+a[5]=1+2=3
=====
n,k=map(int,input().split())
l=list(map(int,input().split()))
c=t=0
for i in range(len(l)):
    for j in range(len(l)):
        if i<j:
            t=l[i]+l[j]
            if t%k==0:
                c=c+1
print(c)


